  "_meta": {
    "description": "Maps Obsidian project folder names to keyword patterns for person-project inference. Keywords are matched against goals, actions, and meeting topics with WORD BOUNDARIES (\\bkeyword\\b) \u2014 not bare substrings. All-caps keywords of <=5 chars are treated as acronyms and matched case-SENSITIVELY. Before 2026-08-24 matching was a bare case-insensitive substring test, which tagged 'Anthropic billing review' as people-ops (the 'hr' inside Anthropic) and 'dashboard redesign' as board-intelligence (the 'board' inside dashboard). Keep keywords >=5 chars or multi-word where possible; a short generic word will still match its own boundary-delimited use. KEYWORDS ARE MATCHED AGAINST REAL DATA (goals, actions, meeting topics) and the KEYS ARE OBSIDIAN FOLDER NAMES \u2014 changing either changes behaviour, so never edit this file as documentation. On 2026-08-30 two person-name keywords were removed from nsls-ceo-transition because this repository is PUBLIC and they named two individuals; the remaining five keywords still cover the project, and a match needs 3 hits to be 'confirmed' either way.",
    "last_updated": "2026-08-24"
  },
